<title>USA: TABLE - Merrill Lynch &amp; Co sells notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Merrill Lynch &amp; Co sells notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK, Date</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc was priced on Tuesday, according to sole manager of the deal, Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>The deal was increased to $500 million from an initial $300 million in size, due to strong demand, according to a market source.</p>
<p>BORROWER MERRILL LYNCH &amp; CO INC</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	 COUPON 6.55 PCT   MATURITY 8/1/2004</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD  6.55 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AA-MINUS  SPREAD +48 BPS    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
